notes: >
  Vendored instead of pip-installed because uni2ts's published pins
  (torch<2.5, numpy~=1.26.0, datasets~=2.17.1) conflict with this project's
  dependencies. Not used for its published pretrained checkpoints; this
  project trains Moirai 2.0 Small from a random initialization on
  GiftEvalPretrain, per the "reduced/from-scratch configuration" pattern
  used for the other TSFM adapters in this project (see
  notes/agentic_logs/2026-08-10-chronos2-loss-space-integration.md).

  Intentional deviations from upstream, applied uniformly across every
  vendored file:

  1. All `jaxtyping` shape-annotated types (`Float[...]`, `Bool[...]`,
     `Int[...]`) were replaced with plain `torch.Tensor` type hints, and the
     `jaxtyping` import was dropped. jaxtyping is not a project dependency
     and these annotations are not enforced at runtime; this is a pure
     type-annotation change with no effect on behavior.
  2. Absolute imports (`uni2ts.module.*`, `uni2ts.common.*`) were rewritten
     to relative imports within this vendored package.

  Additional deviations, scoped to individual files:

  - ts_embed.py: dropped MultiInSizeLinear, FeatLinear, MultiOutSizeLinear,
    and fs2idx (unused surface area for multi-variate/multi-patch-size
    forecasting support that this project's single-patch-size, univariate
    setup never exercises). Only ResidualBlock, used by module.py's
    in_proj/out_proj, is kept.
  - position/__init__.py: dropped the `.additive` import (LearnedEmbedding,
    SinusoidalPositionEncoding), which is unused by Moirai2Module (it only
    uses BinaryAttentionBias for variate attention bias and RotaryProjection
    for time position encoding, per the official module_kwargs). additive.py
    itself was not vendored.
  - torch_util.py: kept only packed_attention_mask, packed_causal_attention_mask,
    and safe_div, the functions Moirai2Module's forward pass and
    PackedStdScaler actually call. Dropped mask_fill, size_to_mask,
    fixed_size, sized_mean, masked_mean, unsqueeze_trailing_dims, and
    numpy_to_torch_dtype_dict (unused once MultiInSizeLinear/etc. above are
    dropped).

  - attention.py: passes zero dropout to PyTorch's scaled dot-product
    attention when the module is in evaluation mode. PyTorch applies the
    supplied dropout probability regardless of module mode.

  All other vendored files (module.py, packed_scaler.py, norm.py,
  transformer.py, ffn.py, position/attn_bias.py,
  position/attn_projection.py) are otherwise byte-for-byte translations of
  upstream, differing only in the two uniform deviations above (jaxtyping
  removal, relative imports). Unused classes within those files (e.g.
  MultiHeadAttention, MultiQueryAttention, RelativeAttentionBias,
  LinearAttentionBias, MoEFeedForward) were kept for fidelity even though
  the small Moirai2 config this project builds does not instantiate them.
